Negative control for the display cluster the rulings replaced D4 with.

D4 — filters, the view toggle and Add new on ONE row — is dead: G3 moved the
ordering onto the data surface, G4 took the collection's own control out to the
page header, G5 gave the refinements a row of their own and H1 sent the count to
Results. This patch restores exactly that superseded layout: one flowing row,
the refinements row gone, and Add new back in the display cluster it left.

Nothing else moves — the same controls, bound the same way, one row instead of
three.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the toolbar-row spec — the surface draws the facets, the refinements they
produced and the display row as three rows of one cluster, and the collection's
own control is NOT among them (it is published to the page that renders it).

